# =============================================================================
# Job Paglu - repository ignore rules
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose: keep secrets, build output and machine-local junk out of git while
# keeping every piece of documentation and every *.example template tracked.
#
# HOW TO READ THIS FILE
#   In .gitignore the LAST matching pattern wins. That is why the broad secret
#   patterns come first and the explicit negations (`!.env.example`) come at the
#   very bottom. Moving a negation above the pattern it re-includes silently
#   breaks it. If you add a new broad pattern, add it ABOVE the negation block.
#
# NOTE FOR NOW (pre-split): this directory currently sits inside a parent
#   workspace whose own .gitignore ignores `.env*` and `*.env` globally, and the
#   parent's rules are what git actually enforces today. Until this directory
#   becomes the root of github.com/job-paglu/homepage, `git status` can hide
#   files that this file deliberately tracks. See scripts/README.md ->
#   "Inherited .gitignore" for what to expect before and after the split.
# =============================================================================


# --- Secrets: environment files ----------------------------------------------
# Protects: database URLs, session secrets, bootstrap passwords. Nothing in this
# group may ever be committed. `.dev.vars` is kept in the list even though
# Cloudflare is no longer the target (DECISIONS D-20): it costs nothing, and an
# ignore rule for a secret file is the wrong thing to remove speculatively.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# --- Secrets: keys, certificates, service accounts ---------------------------
# Protects: TLS material, SSH keys, any cloud service-account JSON. The
# service-account patterns are name-based because the file is plain .json and no
# extension distinguishes it from harmless config.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*-service-account.json
*service_account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
gcp-credentials.json
gha-creds-*.json
credentials.json
secrets/
.secrets/

# --- Node / Astro ------------------------------------------------------------
# Protects the repo from: dependency trees, build output, and generated types.
# `.astro/` holds `types.d.ts`, regenerated by `astro sync` on every build.
# `.vercel/` is local CLI state (project link, pulled env), not source, and must
# never be committed - `vercel pull` writes environment values into it.
# `.wrangler/` is kept for the same reason `.dev.vars` is.
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.wrangler/
.vercel/
.output/
.netlify/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.yarn/cache/
.yarn/install-state.gz

# --- Vite / Vitest caches ----------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated on demand; committing them causes spurious diffs and stale builds.
.vite/
node_modules/.vite/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# --- Go ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Protects the repo from: compiled binaries and test/coverage artefacts.
# Go binaries have no extension on Linux, so they are matched by name/location
# rather than by suffix. `backend/bin/` is where scripts/migrate.* builds the
# server binary it needs in order to run the embedded migration runner.
backend/bin/
backend/server
backend/adminctl
/server
/adminctl
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.txt
cover.html
go.work
go.work.sum

# `vendor/` is NOT used by this project (module cache + go.sum are enough).
# Uncommented deliberately as documentation: if vendoring is ever adopted the
# directory should be COMMITTED, so this line must stay disabled.
# vendor/

# --- Docker / local data -----------------------------------------------------
# Compose keeps Postgres data in a named volume, not a bind mount, so nothing
# should appear here. These patterns catch the case where someone switches to a
# bind mount for debugging and forgets to switch back.
.docker/
docker-compose.override.yml
pgdata/
postgres-data/
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# --- Editors and IDEs --------------------------------------------------------
# `.vscode/*` and not `.vscode/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY has been excluded, so `.vscode/` here would make the
# `!.vscode/extensions.json` negation at the bottom silently ineffective.
# Excluding the directory's CONTENTS instead leaves the negation able to work.
.vscode/*
.idea/
*.iml
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.history/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# --- OS junk -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
*.tmp
*.local
*.log
!scripts/*.log.example


# =============================================================================
# NEGATIONS - these files ARE tracked. They must stay below every pattern above,
# because the last matching pattern wins.
#
# `.env.*` above would otherwise swallow the two template files that are the
# only documentation of which variables exist.
# =============================================================================
!.env.example
!frontend/.env.example
!.dev.vars.example
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.gitkeep
!.editorconfig
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Documentation must never be ignorable by accident.
!README.md
!LICENSE
!docs/
!docs/**
!**/*.md
